    "summary": "I built a compact desk unit with 18 parts: 3 bases, 1 drawer, a spike holding a small platform, 9 end caps and 3 joint bolts. Two full bases (at 0,0 and 1,0) and a north half base (at 0,1) sit in a triangle, so all three meet at one corner. The drawer sits on the cut face of the half base. A mount spike with a small platform stands at the corner where the three bases meet. I closed every open face with an end cap and bolted the joints. The final check found no rule issues and no mesh collisions. I didn't add any props, since the brief only asked for the parts.\n\nTwo attempts were refused along the way. A south half base put the drawer in the corner where the spike stands (SPIKE_CLASH), so I switched to the north half. A solid spike can't carry a platform (TYPE_NOT_ALLOWED), so I used a mount spike.",
